<title>INDIA: India clears NDDB's Sri Lanka joint venture.</title>
<headline>India clears NDDB's Sri Lanka joint venture.</headline>
<dateline>NEW DELHI 1996-10-10</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Indian cabinet has approved a proposal of the state-supported National Dairy Development Board (NDDB) to set up a joint venture with the Sri Lankan government, a government statement said on Thursday.</p>
<p>The government has allowed NDDB to hold upto 51 percent equity in the proposed joint venture, it said.</p>
<p>No further details about the joint venture were given.</p>
</text>
